Lines 41-42 just use the seed to create a random number generator that will be used later to simulate noise for this example. They are not relevant to your own algorithm.

You said that your instances are defined as "--pair_number 0", so in your case, argv[4] will be "--pair_number" and argv[5] will be 0. atoi("--pair_number") will not work. Could that be what is failing in your code?

You need to check your input arguments to be sure that they are what you expect and give a clear error if not. Otherwise locating where the error is in your code will be very hard.

Cheers,

Manuel.

